\begin{didyouknow}{Counting Nodes}
In the 1830s Charles Sturm and Joseph Liouville proved that for a large class of one-dimensional wave equations, the $n$-th eigenfunction, counting from $n=0$, has exactly $n$ zeros inside the interval. This oscillation theorem is why the ground state of any 1D potential well has no nodes, the first excited state has one, and so on. They proved it long before quantum mechanics existed.
\end{didyouknow}
