\begin{didyouknow}{Can You Hear a Drum?}
Hermann Weyl proved in 1911 that the number of vibration modes of a drum below a given frequency grows in proportion to its area. In 1966 Mark Kac asked whether the full list of frequencies determines the drum's shape. In 1992 Carolyn Gordon, David Webb and Scott Wolpert answered no by constructing two differently shaped drums with identical spectra. Level counts reveal a lot, but not everything.
\end{didyouknow}
